@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second plan review PASS, blocking=0. The sole P6 advisory is accepted without another plan mutation: the two flagged lines each name one document-content contract whose terms must coexist in the same ADR section (mixed-version protocol plus its rollout gate; measured evidence plus its provenance), and execution will verify every named token independently. Plan signature is current at 1d136b8db5.","timestamp":1785805278218406001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"ADR draft created in isolated worktree /Users/joeoakhart/impl-0303-a5 at docs/adr/0059-bridge-state-format-changes.md. It covers A1/A2/A3/A4-2, committed-on-branch durability, chronological-max expand/contract, sidecar-first failure ordering, direct A2-2 deployment evidence, pass-record insufficiency, per-change rollback limits, raw assignee rationale, 12.79 KB -> 1.74 KB and 218/399 measurements, session log provenance, docs/migrations.md/352b and canonical epic 6c9c-811f-6dc4-40e7 prior art. Deterministic content checks, merged-commit ancestry checks, docs/README directory-link check, git diff --check, make lint, and make typecheck pass. Full-suite evidence remains before commit.","timestamp":1785805625298800001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Current main assigned ADR 0059 to the LLM provider seam while A5 was in flight. Renamed this ADR to the next available sequential number, docs/adr/0060-bridge-state-format-changes.md, updated its heading and ticket material, and fast-forwarded the worktree to c1f1179b59. No decision content changed.","timestamp":1785813051541538001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"A5 validation and review milestone: deterministic ADR acceptance checks, plan status, lint, and typecheck are green. F